# Orbits Holepunch invariants

Phase 0 is locked in `docs/migration/`. Default transport is still PeerJS.

- Identity (`identity-signing-v1`, X3DH, Double Ratchet) is not the Hyperswarm Noise key.
- Hypercore stores encrypted envelopes only — never plaintext, KEK, ratchet scalars, or discovery secrets.
- Drift is a local read-model after decrypt. Do not make it the sync source of truth.
- Discovery topic is `HASH("orbits-contact-discovery-v1" || sharedSecret)`. Never `HASH(peerId)`.
- Block list runs before decrypt and before Drift persist.
- Rooms stay host-plaintext. Do not flip `kRoomsApplicationE2eImplemented` or add `room_crypto.dart`.
- `HyperswarmRollout` defaults to `off`. Do not wire Hyperswarm into `ConnectionsNotifier` until Phase 4.
- Production Bare must not fetch remote executable JS.
- Do not run device / NAT / Kazakhstan hardware matrices unless the user is free and asks.
- Product files are the Dart `FileTransferCoordinator` (`orbits-file-v1`, 64 KiB frames via `transport.send`); Bare/plugin `sendFile` is harness-only. Whole-file `Uint8List` payloads never cross IPC in one frame, and a native send failure stays `pending` + `lastReplicationError` (never whole-file base64 / PeerJS fallback).
